{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101874","id":2289843404,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6IfDzM","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101874","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101874.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101874.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101874","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101874/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101874/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101874/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/bdd51cfa1441cedcf0d9cd9c4d824ee4f77bf3ff","number":101874,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add `is_trivially_relocatable` struct to facilitate reasoning about trivial relocatability.","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Trivial relocatability describes whether an object can be _moved_ to a different address without invalidating its invariants.\r\nFor more information on trivial relocatability, see https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/docs/papers/2023/p1144r7.html and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100509. \r\n\r\nTrivial relocatability can be used to improve performance, especially for vector-like types. Notably, it is assumed to be 'always true' in some parts of our codebase (see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100509).\r\n\r\nThis PR is the first step for addressing https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100509 by allowing us to reason about it at all.\r\n\r\n## Caveats\r\nIn the current implementation, trivial relocatability is eagerly `true` for all types except trivially copyable types. This matches the current behavior of types where this is relevant (see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100509).\r\nIt would be possible to instead choose the safe, conservative approach of defaulting to `false` (or better, `is_trivially_copyable`). A more complex implementation might even try to figure out trivial relocatability in a more advanced way ([reference folly](https://github.com/facebook/folly/blob/859ce5ae782145a3f6803c54caa1741475db4018/folly/Traits.h#L702-L714)). \r\n\r\nHowever, given that our current codebase seems to be _fairly safe_ w.r.t. trivial relocatability, I think we should try to avoid performance regressions by defaulting to `true`.\r\n\r\n## Usage Guide\r\n\r\nTo reference this information, reference the following code example:\r\n```c++\r\nif constexpr (is_trivially_relocatable<T>) {\r\n    buf_ptr = Memory::realloc_static(ptr, alloc_size, false);\r\n}\r\nelse {\r\n   T *new_buf_ptr = Memory::alloc_static(alloc_size, false);\r\n    for (int i = 0; i < size(); i++) {\r\n        new_buf_ptr[i] = std::move(buf_ptr[i]);\r\n    }\r\n    Memory::free_static(buf_ptr, false);\r\n    buf_ptr = new_buf_ptr;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlternatively, a type can be marked unsafe for nontrivial relocatability by using SFINAE:\r\n```c++\r\ntemplate <typename T, typename = std::enable_if_t<is_trivially_relocatable<T>>\r\nstruct CowData {\r\n    // ...\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo mark a struct as not trivially relocatable, reference the following code:\r\n```c++\r\nstruct is_trivially_relocatable<MyStruct> : std::false_type {};\r\n```\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","description":"","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-01-21T12:19:25Z","updated_at":"2025-02-12T17:14:59Z","closed_at":"2025-02-12T16:58:49Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"60703e48dc35217840c055d4529247a808867cd0","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Ivorforce:is_trivially_relocatable","ref":"is_trivially_relocatable","repo":{"id":861387944,"node_id":"R_kgDOM1e8qA","name":"godot","full_name":"Ivorforce/godot","owner":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/